 result←object(State Color)arg;was;t
 result←⍬
 ⍝ 'Color' colorBack [colorText]

 :If 0=≢arg ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Empty command is ignored
 :If 1≥|≡arg ⍝ If it's simple, nest it like we expect (un-Single it)
     :If 6=≢arg ⋄ arg←(3/1 2)⊆arg ⋄ :Else ⋄ arg←,⊂arg ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ But two RGBs may be conjoined and we want to separate them
 :EndIf
 'DOMAIN ERROR'##.Error 2<≢arg ⍝ Too many argument items?
 '∆WI LENGTH ERROR: Color'##.Error∨/~(≢¨arg)∊¨⊂0 1 3
 '∆WI DOMAIN ERROR: Color'##.Error∨/1<|≡¨arg

 was←State._color_ ⍝ What's our previous (parsed) color?
 :If ∨/t←1=≢¨arg←,¨arg ⋄ (t/arg)←⊃¨t/arg ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ De-ravel singletons, for comfort
 :If ∨/t←0=≢¨arg ⋄ (t/arg)←t/was ⋄ :EndIf ⍝ Fill in previous-defaults
 arg,←arg≢⍛↓was ⍝ Fill in any elided trailing items
 {}State(##.Classes.color ChangeError'color' 'Color')arg ⍝ Call the standard property fn to make assignments directly into our current State
